-  Coverage counts only nodes that pass.
+  Coverage counts only nodes that pass. To keep `map` to minutes on large animated decks, up to 24 runs are written at once, each with a sentinel of its own (`⟦bl1⟧`, `⟦bl2⟧`…), and checked on one load against step 4 with their own sentinel; then the writes are undone newest first and the bytes compared. Whatever a batch cannot attribute to one run (a new console error, a changed slide count, a refused write, a failed undo), and every run that fails on a batch, is probed again on its own with `⟦bl⟧`, and that result stands.
